Z||000040||ferrari_momo||11-07-2001||10:03 PM||||Hello friends,<BR> if you notice the gray primered area. that is the whole unit to this kit.  It is one big piece.  I left the rest of the car red, so that you can see where the seperations will be.  That is your seperating point.  The lens will use 80-82 vette lens.  Unless if i can make some deals w/ Ausfiero in the near future.  the hole is 5" diameter.  As soon as this is all done, i will have one installed on one of my prototype car and Josh's car(JCH82 will have installation manual w/ pics made, LOL).  But this has been carefully thought of.  This version of taillight kit will go up with the deck lid.  It will look something like Grand Prix or Cadillac, etc.  Wiring will be up and down with the deck lid.  This first version is a bit challenging.  It would be good for any handly person.   I hope this version will be in demand for those who love the challenges.  Prices on this version will be lower than the screw on, 2nd version.  <BR>  The final version (3rd prototype notchback euro) will be bonded on the the body.  Where the deck lid will be left alone.  But deck lid cover will have a piece of finishing lip.  The 3rd version may be slightly wider.  And a new bumper will be in design to accomodate that new taillight.  I am hoping to illuminate the black moldings around the car.  Let's get the 2002 look at these awesome fieros. AYE?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> hehehe<BR>thank u y'all.<BR>pat kalsmith<BR><P>------------------<BR>||||reg||10
Z||000041||BC-GT||11-07-2001||11:59 PM||||BC-GT busts out his most impressive photoshop skills to see what these would look like on his wheels??<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/picture/sraid27/pc7bcf4f854435c7c25e306b6d66ec193/fe24845e.jpg.orig.jpg"> <BR>Bursts out laughing, while looking for his "Idiot's Guide to Photoshop Manual"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_wtf.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Darryl Martin<BR>1985 GT <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.imagestation.com/picture/pf251a969c96964ef15691e97e7ac4489/feb64e3a.jpg.orig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000042||Smoooooth GT||11-08-2001||07:30 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fieroX:<BR><B>   I was thinking a rear fascia with a shaved exhaust outlet so it is the same height all the way across but have 2 of these holes cut on each side to integrate the exhaust into the rear fascia.  That would be awesome.  I think im going to work it up in photoshop and see what happens. <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>Like this?? Here's mine now without the exhaust .. exhaust will be coming outta the side...Sorry sooo big..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/wing_from_rear_3.JPG"> <P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Smooooth_Yellow_sig_3.gif">   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig_blue_3.gif"> ||||reg||1
